@page "/how-to-play"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@inject NavigationManager NavigationManager

<div class="container">
    <div class="card">
        <div class="card-header">
            <p class="eyebrow">The rules</p>
            <h1>🔎 How to play Undercover</h1>
        </div>

        <div class="prose">
            <h4>Overview</h4>
            <p>Undercover is a pass-and-play social deduction game. Each player gets a secret card: most hold the civilian word, one or more hold a similar-but-different undercover word, and Mr. White gets no word at all. Players take turns saying one word linked to their secret, then the group discusses and votes someone out.</p>

            <h4>Step by step</h4>
            <ol>
                <li>Pick a word category, set the number of players, and add everyone's name.</li>
                <li>Pass the device around. Each player picks a card and reveals it privately — only Mr. White is told they are Mr. White; civilians and undercover just see a word.</li>
                <li>Following the speaking order, everyone says one word relating to their secret word.</li>
                <li>After everyone has spoken, start voting. The group votes out the player they think is Undercover or Mr. White.</li>
                <li>If Mr. White is voted out, they get one guess at the civilian word: right and they win the round, wrong and they're eliminated.</li>
                <li>Play continues until the civilians eliminate every Undercover and Mr. White, the Undercover reach parity, or Mr. White guesses correctly.</li>
            </ol>

            <h4>Scoring</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Civilians win: every surviving Civilian gets <strong>+1 point</strong>.</li>
                <li>Undercover / Mr. White win: every surviving Undercover or Mr. White gets <strong>+1 point</strong>.</li>
                <li>Mr. White is voted out and guesses the civilian word: they win the round solo for <strong>+3 points</strong>.</li>
                <li>Scores add up across "Next round" and reset with "New game".</li>
            </ul>

            <h4>Tips</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Keep your clue short and not too revealing.</li>
                <li>Mr. White should stay general and echo the mood of the room.</li>
                <li>Discuss before you vote — one bad vote can hand the round to the Undercover.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="action-bar">
            <a class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg" href="https://github.com/ArdonToonstra/undercover-game/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Report an issue</a>
            <button class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" @onclick='() => NavigationManager.NavigateTo(NavigationManager.BaseUri, false)'>Back to game</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

